---
/**
 * Fixed banner at the top of every research page.
 *
 * ResearchLayout renders this directly rather than exposing it as a slot, so an
 * individual page cannot omit it.
 *
 * On the wording: an earlier draft read "There is nothing to obtain here."
 * That was accurate when compiler/ held a licence file and nothing else. It no
 * longer is — the toolchain's source is in the repository, 336 files with a
 * README that documents how to build it against a local LLVM. What remains true,
 * and what the banner has to say instead, is the distribution claim: nothing is
 * packaged, and none of the four channels carry it. That is also exactly what
 * the `Research` status means here — the test is whether one URL gets you the
 * thing today, and cloning a repository and building a Clang plugin is not that.
 */
---

<aside class="vg-research-banner" role="note">
  <span class="vg-badge vg-badge--research">Research</span>
  <p>
    An ongoing research project, written up as a paper. There is no released build of
    this and none of the VibeGuard channels include it — the source lives in the
    repository and is built against a local LLVM.
  </p>
</aside>
